                <pb facs="0837" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 212.11G16/13.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Wilson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-06-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 101.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 86, of the 8th instant,
                    and to my telegram of to-day, I have the honor to inclose, for the department’s
                    information, copy and translation of a note received to-day from the foreign
                    office, and copy of my reply thereto, relative to the provisional arrest and
                    detention of Heliodoro Garcia, charged with assault with intent to commit murder
                    in California.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>




